                <mxCell id="ANET" value="Internet → OpenAI" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#7a2e2b;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1380" y="600" width="160" height="60" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="Anote" value="AWS (Track B). Delivery layer only differs from Local:&#xa;SQS → Lambda replaces the poll loop; process_job is&#xa;identical. Query = hybrid ANN + BM25 → RRF.&#xa;&#xa;Egress: both Lambdas embed via OpenAI (API = query,&#xa;worker = docs). All private-subnet egress (OpenAI ·&#xa;SQS send · SSM · CloudWatch) traverses the NAT&#xa;instance → Internet Gateway; only S3 uses the free&#xa;S3 gateway endpoint. Add SQS/SSM/Logs interface&#xa;endpoints to cut NAT traffic.&#xa;&#xa;Config in Parameter Store. Secrets (OpenAI key,&#xa;DB password) in Secrets Manager; both read by the&#xa;Lambdas, EC2 reads only the DB password.&#xa;CloudWatch collects Lambda logs. Worker reads PDFs from S3, extracting&#xa;via pdfplumber → OCR (pytesseract) → Claude (sparse).&#xa;Backups: nightly pg_dump → S3 + daily EBS&#xa;snapshots (DLM, keep 7).&#xa;&#xa;Omitted for clarity: Reconciler Lambda (EventBridge,&#xa;15 min) that re-enqueues stuck / undelivered jobs." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#555555;fontStyle=0;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="940" y="44" width="380" height="345" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e0" value="HTTPS" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;strokeColor=#333333;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" source="A1" target="A2" edge="1">
